[
    {
        "content": "<p>I am hitting a timeout when synthesizing <code>Module ↥E' ↥(E' ⊔ F')</code> where <code>E'</code> and <code>F'</code> are <code>extendScalars</code> of intermediate fields with a local <code>Algebra ↥E' ↥(E' ⊔ F')</code> instance in context</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">FieldTheory</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">LinearDisjoint</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Field</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Field</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IntermediateField</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↥</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊓</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↥</span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">IntermediateField</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">inclusion</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inf_le_left</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toRingHom</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toAlgebra</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IntermediateField</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↥</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊓</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">extendScalars</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊓</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inf_le_left</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IntermediateField</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↥</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊓</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">extendScalars</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊓</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inf_le_right</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↥</span><span class=\"n\">E'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↥</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">E'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F'</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">IntermediateField</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">inclusion</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le_sup_left</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toRingHom</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toAlgebra</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">finrank</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↥</span><span class=\"n\">E'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↥</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">E'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F'</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">trivial</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The analogous situation with <code>Subalgebra</code> works fine. From trace analysis, the <code>Subalgebra</code> version succeeds because <code>Subalgebra.moduleLeft</code> appears in the candidates list and provides a cheap path. <code>IntermediateField</code> has no such instance and adding an analog  instance seems to help partially but does not fix the timeout. The  bottleneck appears to be a repeated expensive check (~167K heartbeats each) involving <code>Field.toSemifield.toCommSemiring =?= SubsemiringClass.toCommSemiring</code>, which is triggered each time Lean needs to verify that a term has type <code>IntermediateField (↥(E ⊓ F)) L</code>.</p>\n<p>I am aware that the construction is somewhat convoluted, but this is the natural setup that arises in the proof I am working on and I do not see a way to avoid it. Is there anything I can do to work around this?</p>",
        "id": 599148156,
        "sender_full_name": "Xavier Roblot",
        "timestamp": 1780317700
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It does work if you remove the line <code>let : Algebra ↥(E ⊓ F) ↥E := (IntermediateField.inclusion inf_le_left).toRingHom.toAlgebra</code></p>",
        "id": 599149026,
        "sender_full_name": "Sébastien Gouëzel",
        "timestamp": 1780317931
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Oh, sorry. I spent a long time tracing 30 million heartbeats when the fix was removing one line <span aria-label=\"man facepalming\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f926-200d-2642\" role=\"img\" title=\"man facepalming\">:man_facepalming:</span></p>",
        "id": 599150046,
        "sender_full_name": "Xavier Roblot",
        "timestamp": 1780318215
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think it's not the end of the story: the line you wrote doesn't work well because some things in there are not reducible enough. It would probably be worth it putting <code>fast_instance%</code> on <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Algebra.instSubtypeMemSubalgebraMin#doc\">docs#Algebra.instSubtypeMemSubalgebraMin</a>, and/or making <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=IntermediateField.inclusion#doc\">docs#IntermediateField.inclusion</a> more reducible, or whatever. I've never played with algebras in Mathlib, so I'd let experts chime in.</p>",
        "id": 599151210,
        "sender_full_name": "Sébastien Gouëzel",
        "timestamp": 1780318510
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You can try <code>relrank</code> but it is also a mess...</p>",
        "id": 599205073,
        "sender_full_name": "Jz Pan",
        "timestamp": 1780331829
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Note that <code>RingHom.toAlgebra</code> has a warning in the docstring, and you did not heed this warning: there is already an instance of <code>SMul ↥(E ⊓ F) ↥E</code>. Ironically it comes from the algebra instance which already exists, so you made a diamond with this code.</p>",
        "id": 599210556,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1780333465
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You're right, I paid the price for not reading the docstring! In my (weak) defense, the sup case worked fine with RingHom.toAlgebra, so I thought I was safe. Only when Sébastien told me, I realized inf already had an algebra instance waiting to create a diamond.</p>",
        "id": 599213450,
        "sender_full_name": "Xavier Roblot",
        "timestamp": 1780334346
    }
]